 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "sessions is a list of strings \"<user_id>,<input_tokens>,<output_tokens>,<plan>\" with canonical decimal token counts. pricing is a list of comma-separated plan rows; every plan used by a session has exactly one row. Prices are non-negative integers in an abstract smallest currency unit per token, so every amount is an exact integer. Return [user_id, total] for every user that has at least one session, sorted by user_id in code-point order. Level 2: a pricing row is \"<plan>,<input_price>,<output_price>,<monthly_fee>,<included_tokens>\". For every (user, plan) pair that has at least one session, the user pays monthly_fee once and has included_tokens free tokens on that plan. Sessions are processed in list order; within a session the input tokens use the remaining free tokens first, then the output tokens; only tokens beyond the allowance are charged at their price.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk09-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
